# 🧠 INTELLIGENT TECH STACK SELECTION (MANDATORY)

Before implementation:

## STEP 1 – Analyze Repository

You must identify:

- Backend language (Java / Node / .NET / Python / Go etc.)
- Framework (Spring Boot / Express / NestJS / ASP.NET etc.)
- Architecture (Monolith / Microservices)
- API type (REST / GraphQL / WebSocket)
- Authentication mechanism
- Deployment model
- Target audience (Admin / Internal / Public app)

Summarize findings.

Wait for approval.

---

## STEP 2 – Select Best UI Stack Based on Project Context

Default priority order:

### Standard Enterprise Backend (Spring Boot / Node / .NET REST)
→ React + TypeScript (Vite)

### SEO-sensitive public application
→ Next.js + TypeScript (SSR/SSG)

### GraphQL-heavy system
→ Next.js + Apollo Client

### Large enterprise ecosystem (.NET-heavy org)
→ React + TypeScript (preferred)
→ Angular only if ecosystem already uses it

### Internal Admin Dashboard
→ React + TypeScript + Tailwind or Material UI

### Lightweight internal tool
→ Vite + React + TypeScript

Non-negotiable:
- TypeScript mandatory
- Strict mode enabled
- No plain JavaScript

