# 🔌 API CONSUMPTION RULES

- Do NOT modify API response models
- Do NOT assume fields that do not exist
- Always inspect backend DTOs before consuming
- Centralize API calls in `src/api`
- Use typed API clients
- Handle:
  - Loading states
  - Error states
  - Retry logic
  - Empty states
- Do not hardcode URLs
- Use environment variables

Never hallucinate endpoints.

---

# 🎨 UI/UX STANDARDS

- Fully responsive
- Clean modern layout
- Reusable components
- No inline styles
- Utility-based styling (Tailwind preferred) or Material UI
- Accessibility compliant
- Proper spacing system
- Skeleton loaders
- Error boundaries
- Dark mode support (optional but preferred)

---

# 🔐 AUTHENTICATION HANDLING

If backend provides authentication:

- Integrate using existing endpoints
- Do NOT modify token generation logic
- Store tokens securely
- Support refresh tokens if available
- Implement route protection

Do not redesign auth logic.

---

